# Grid A — S11 Boolean / Existence (tool-call gating)
#
# Targets: ShapeBoolean + generic scenario. The answer must be
# a clear yes/no, not a hedge. Question targets a known hard rule:
# evidence-lite pre-scan explicitly FORBIDS read_file at stage=analyze,
# and validateAnalyzerPrescanToolCall is the enforcer.
#
# Ground truth (internal/agent/agent.go + analyzer_classification_grep_test.go):
# the analyzer cannot call read_file. Correct answer is "no". Positive
# anchor keeps the answer anchored on the check function. Negative
# anchors block the classic hedge phrases that mean the LLM didn't
# actually verify.
ID="s11a"
NAME="boolean — does the analyzer stage allow read_file?"
QUESTION="Explorer stage 之前的 analyzer stage 里是否允许调用 read_file？"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC `analyze read_file` was
# the question's two keywords — bar = "复述题目"; a generic "yes
# the analyzer can call read_file" PASSed without the truthful
# answer ("no"). Strengthen by requiring the answer to surface
# (a) a negative verdict (no/forbidden/not allowed/禁止/不允许)
# AND (b) the enforcer's name (validateAnalyzerPrescanToolCall),
# proving the answer reached the actual gate logic.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="analyze read_file validateAnalyzerPrescanToolCall"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(\bno\b|not allowed|forbidden|禁止|不允许|不能)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="it.depends sometimes maybe"
